_ _____            _________________ __ _
 ______) OVERVIEW (________________ _

noC-WHO is the one of most full-featured and flexible WHO doors available, from 
both the  standpoint  of  the  SYSOP  and the USER.  Following is a list of what 
is available in this version:
 
   * SIMPLE TO INSTALL - ONE DOOR...
   * Compatible with V3.3x+ (32 node version) and pre-v3.3 /X (10 node version)
     and Sigma Express.
   * Users may choose & SAVE their design preference.
   * Sysops can appoint PRIVILEGED users who can:
       * Change their action field.
       * See EVERYTHING.
       * Constantly monitor nodes using the update option.
   * A miscellaneous field is available for the sysop to configure as he likes.
   * All action texts are configurable.
   * Several sysop options.
   * This door, unlike many others, knows when OTHERS are using it.
   * Calls per day are known WITHOUT any additional doors, and are
     reset at midnight automatically.  
   * noC-WHO is compatible with all future nocTurne deSign products.
   * Much more.  And the future is even better.  READ ON..

_ _____                _________________ __ _
 ______) INSTALLATION (________________ _

noC-WHO  is  compatible  with  Ami-Express  versions  2.xx thru 3.xx and Sigma
Express.   Follow the conventional door installation methods for your version.
Throw the "noC-WHO" directory into "Doors:" and you are set.  To customize the
door continue reading.

To  define  the  available  settings   for   noC-WHO,   edit   the   text file
"Doors:noC-WHO/who.config".    The  following parameters may be set within the
configuration file:

SYSOP_ACTION=[TEXT]  :  Some  sysops like to have themselves listed on a local
                        node.  This parameter allows them to customize exactly 
                        what their ACTION field says.  
                        (Example: "SYSOP_ACTION=Hanging in the John.")

FILENAMES_DISABLED=[YES/NO] : If you want that filenames be listed with Upload
                              and Download actions, set this to YES.

DIVIDERS_DISABLED=[YES/NO] : If you have more than 6 nodes or so, you may want
                             to DISABLE  the DIVIDING LINES between node texts
                             to make the display more COMPACT.

PUBLIC_UPDATE=[YES/NO] : Some sysops  may not want  the  general  public to be
                         able to  use the 'WHO U' option to CONSTANTLY MONITOR
                         other nodes, and can use this option to DISABLE it.
                            
COOLUSER.[NUM] : Trusted users should be listed with this parameter. They will
                 be able to see EVERYTHING  and have  privileged access to the
                 door.  (Example: "COOLUSER.1=nocTurne COOLUSER.2=john")
                 
MISC.TITLE=[TEXT] : noC-WHO  features  a  configurable column of  8 characters
                    width on the far right  of the  display.   To define  this
                    field for your OWN purposes you must first create a title.
                    (Example: "MISC.TITLE=Fone Num")
                    
MISC.[NUM] : You may  define what is printed in the configurable field of EACH
             node  using  this option.   You may  list ringdown numbers, modem
             types, or whatever you WANT,  But remember: 8 characters MAX.  If
             you want any of them to display the BAUD, set them to '@'.
             (Example: "MISC.0=LOCAL MISC.1=555-1212 MISC.2=555-1213" )
             
If  you  want  to  customize  the  action  texts  you  must can edit the texts
proceeding  the  "@BEGIN_ACTIONS"  string  in  the config file.  These are the
default  texts  for every action, (Awaiting call, Beginning UL, etc...).  When
you EDIT these texts, be sure to keep them under around 18 characters and KEEP
THEM  IN  THE ORDER THEY CAME.  Any additional carriage returns or alterations
to the arrangement of the file may result in incorrect action displays.

If you are using Files-Reverse (V1.0+), set the "NocWhoCompat=" in the door's
icon to "YES".  FR will then be recognized by noC-WHO when it is in use. This
feature will be available in all FUTURE doors by nocTurne deSign.

The  DEFAULT  SETTINGS  for  noC-WHO  if  they  are  not explicitly set in the
configuration file are as follows:

            FILENAMES_DISABLED = NO
            DIVIDERS_DISABLED  = YES
            PUBLIC_UPDATE      = YES
            MISC.TITLE         = Baud
            MISC.[NUM's]       = [Each users' connect rate]
    
_ _____         _________________ __ _
 ______) USAGE (________________ _

Information  on  program  usage  may  be  obtained with "WHO ?".  To CONFIGURE
noC-WHO to one of the five styles available, the user may enter "WHO E", which
will  prompt  him  to  select his preference.  A DATA FILE with all the users'
preferences  will  be maintained named "DOORS:noC-WHO/data/who-users.dat".  If
the  UPDATE  option  has  been  made  available  to  all users, or the user is
privileged,  he  may  use  this  door to actively monitor the actions of those
online.  "WHO U" will cause noC-WHO to update its display every second until a
key  is  pressed.    If the "PUBLIC_UPDATE" config option is set to "NO", only
privileged  users will be able to have display updates.  Those with privileged
access  may  also set their ACTION text.  Setting it to NOTHING will cause all
actions to be displayed normally.

Nodes  that  are  QUIETED will be EXEMPT from being displayed.  Nodes that are
disabled or unavailable will be shown as such.  At midnight, a task spawned by
the door will automatically reset the call counter to 0.

